cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use OpenVeil, please cite it as below. Each release is archived on
  Zenodo. The concept DOI 10.5281/zenodo.24505557 cites all versions and
  always resolves to the latest one; to cite a specific version, use the
  version DOI shown on the Zenodo record of the version you used (the version
  DOI of 1.1.0 appears on Zenodo after its release). An arXiv preprint
  describing OpenVeil is forthcoming; this file will be updated with its
  reference when it is available. The references below are the case-study
  dataset, its data descriptor and the crop verifier weights.
type: software
title: "OpenVeil: Detect, verify and mosaic people in video datasets before release, with an interactive human review tool"
abstract: >-
  OpenVeil helps researchers release video datasets that show people. It
  proposes person boxes with an open-vocabulary detector, verifies them with a
  fine-tuned crop classifier, lets a human check the hard cases in a local
  review tool, and mosaics the people while re-encoding only the parts of each
  video that contain a mosaic (smart cut).
